seg-7135c6f44d49 = How the accuracy codes are read and the grid and route geometry are <b>VALIDATED</b> against independent libraries on synthetic inputs; the method's thresholds stay <b>MODELLED</b>, and that a degraded cell is interference is <b>not</b> checked: a degraded cell does <b>not</b> identify interference as the cause. A cell not observed is <b>not</b> evidence of a clear route. Past reports, <b>not a forecast</b>. Aggregate only: do not try to recover identifiers. ADS-B and AIS maps stay separate.

# text
seg-e47db9be47ea = Sky geometry, skyline

# text
# c1: advisory
seg-839eb485b1d2 = <b>MODELLED</b> geometry under a stated error model, line of sight only: no diffraction, multipath or non-line-of-sight reception. Presets are <b>REPRESENTATIVE</b>, not surveys; carry the preset's provenance. Preset constellations are a representative sky, not the sky of a date. The ellipse scales a stated UERE: not a measured accuracy and not an integrity bound. Keep the <c1/>.

# text
# c1: optical-atmosphere
seg-0002a3dc682e = Optical-link availability (<c1/>, { "0.37" })

# text
# c1: availability_ceiling_pct
seg-1098f908d9dc = <b>MODELLED</b>, advisory. The cloud climates are stated inputs, not a dataset, and no measured availability record has been compared: say "under these assumptions", never "the availability at that site". Keep the site's <b>ceiling</b> (<c1/>: what no margin lifts) beside its availability, and say which technique gains are inputs (Kshana does not model an adaptive-optics loop). The numerics are checked against an independent program, which checks the implementation of the formulas and not the atmosphere.

