# c1: docs/TIMING-HIL.md
seg-9177789844f7 = <b>MODELLED</b>, advisory. Say "measured against the mask", never that a clock or system meets or is approved against a Recommendation. The two times (GNSS removed, GNSS restored) are the <b>operator's statement</b>: Kshana did not remove or restore anything and cannot verify them, so quote them as stated. A mask the record is too short for is <b>INCOMPLETE</b>, never a pass. A servo log (linuxptp, chrony) is the error under servo control, not an independent measurement against UTC; say which record the figures come from. See <c1/>.

